    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "Well, first of all, let me say this. I'm going to just use this opportunity because I actually, I believe it's, but President Biden doesn't get the full credit. And then tell you what I think is happening, which is he has re-energized alliances. And after a hiatus of that, of actively insecuring and giving our allies the level of insecurity, he has energized alliances. You saw it on massive display at the G7 recently. And he has made, I can at least say in Japan, the allies in the head of state feel incredibly secure. And when that happens, They'll go farther. They won't clear the bar. They'll exceed it. Classic example is Japan and Korea. That reproachments happen before the past, but they are working at a level. All the experts have said, hasn't been seen in over 20 years. I know the Korean Prime Minister, he was the U.S. ambassador for Korea to the United States. We worked through the FTA when I was Chief of Staff. Obviously in Japan, I think we've done a hard work with the government building confidence.",
