    "turn_idx": 71,
    "turn_text": "year. Or he was at least invited. In this count, one of the big things, you can never remember what you're reading on the secret side versus what you read of it, but you gotta remember that. I wouldn't be careful. There isn't a NATO for there. The biggest goal is to get to see Europe have a vested interest in a free and open Indo-Pacific. You have said something about rules-based system. Look, there is a basic assumption, not just the rules. The basic assumptions of rowing, we say, rules based order. Let's unpack that. There's a set of rules that we all basically acknowledge, and that the rules will be applied equally across the waterfront to all of us, and we all abide by enforcing. What has happened is Russia clearly didn't do that in the invasion of Ukraine, because that is the founding principle of the United Nations is you don't obviously take military action on a sovereign nation. China enters the WTO based on rules. They have not stopped their intellectual property espionage and economic espionage. When it came to the conflict on the maritime issues with the Philippines, the Maritime Court ruled against China for the Philippines, China ignored it. When it comes to patents, China ignores it. When it comes to other types of economic, but also military activities. They ignore it. Coercion is a common tool they use to force countries using their economic power to force their political independence to be limited. So you can't have a rules-based system or people part of a system that are refused to abide by the basic principle",
