  {
    "episode_id": 71605,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71605.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 73,
    "turn_text": "So it's not the rules. It's the premise behind the rules, which is they are agreed to. and you abide by them. And with China, Russia, North Korea, Iran have said, we're not going to abide by this, we're not. And they want all the, and the irony is, take China, they have now decided to undermine the very system that benefited. And now you're seeing an economy that has the highest unemployment of youth in any OECD country, massive debt overhang on the public sector, massive empty housing problems, research and development area that's very massively challenged. Why? Because they decided, and capital outflow as well as people outflow. Why? Because they decided to break down the one thing that actually was important to their economic growth.",
