    "turn_text": "failed miserably and that's number one. So when I say unity what China wants is a divided world where they have maximum leverage. What's our ACEs, our alliances, and the more we energize our alliances, and that unity comes from it. It's buried your seed in direct relationship towards going on the battlefield in Ukraine. NATO has spoken with a singular voice, and it has had a tremendous impact on the military outcomes in Europe. That is also true as it relates to China. Now, when China sees that, their choices get limited. Let me give you another example. Three years ago, because the Prime Minister of Australia had the audacity to say we should investigate the foundations of COVID and how it happened. China immediately went to their playbook on economic coercion. barley, wheat, wine, everything. They basically threw in the towels quietly. Why? Because the rest of the world, major economies that Australia trades with, they worked through in a process. They have trade alliance with the United States, with other players in the world. They could adjust. And they not only survived, they thrived. And China basically realized it failed. So unity in collective action, collaborative, cooperative, confronting a China or Russia has a tremendous impact. And that's why China, in my view, as a related to the EU, has failed. As a related to what Australia failed, what Russia just is seeing in Ukraine failed when we act with a singular voice. And it takes a lot of work bringing a lot of disparate voices into some unified fashion. That has an impact. And we see it time again and we actually, every time we have to relearn the lesson. That's the weird part. I want to get back. If I had one thing that I would like to try to get done is for us, our whole country's gone to this notion that economic engagement with the world was a failure. And the truth is, you couldn't have had the Pax Americana in the post-World War II era, not just because we had the largest militaries, but also because we had the largest economy, and we were growing at an unprecedented level. We have incredible strengths. At least in the Indo-Pacific, can't speak to every other president of the world. They want more of America, not less.",
