    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/1/71605.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 181,
    "turn_text": "The way I see it, trade creates a lot of opportunity, but the opportunity is not equally shared. And we have to acknowledge that not everybody wins that trade. You can think about it in macro terms, but not true in micro terms. Number two, risk. If you want a integrated global economy where the United States is integrated, you have to do things where you mitigate risk because they're not equally shared also. So I will just say to you that in the trade area, We in the public sector, while we saw there's a lot of benefits to it, we did not ensure that everybody got an equal chance at those benefits.",
