    "turn_text": "didn't happen. That doesn't mean you end trade. It means you come up with a different model where you get more people that are winners in the winner circle. I would take a policy thing that I'm really proud of that I did, two things. We never had universal full day kindergarten in Chicago. because on the Northside had it, kids thought it was like, you know, made sure that every child in the city should have got a full decantern. We then introduced full day pre-K for every child, seven hours a day. And then we were the first city ever to make community college free. We got to be average. Every child got tuition, books, transportation, fully paid for. Three years, use it, lose it. Starting earlier, going later in life in education's key. And by making sure that high school was not the end of our commitment, but somebody, you had a plan for afterwards. And then changing kids' dynamics. So a lot of kids, like in the city of Chicago, my kids would say, you know, where am I going to be when I'm 21? What am I going to be doing? Some kids never thought they would make it to see the 21st birthday.",
